---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SOCIAL } from '../consts';

const FACTS = [
	['Experience', '10 years across software engineering, applied AI and product development'],
	['Based in', 'Stuttgart area, Germany'],
	['Education', 'MSc Communication Engineering, Technical University of Munich'],
	['Previously', 'Bosch · Mercedes-Benz Tech Motion'],
	['Now', 'Founder of Anovi · Applied AI systems consultant · Independent product engineer'],
	['Core stack', 'Python · TypeScript · React Native · FastAPI · PostgreSQL'],
	[
		'Focus',
		'Production AI · Mobile and backend systems · Zero-to-one products · Technical investigation',
	],
];
---

<Base
	title="About"
	description="Applied AI systems consultant, product engineer and founder. 10 years across embedded engineering, production AI, mobile and backend systems, and shipped products."
	person
>
	<h1>About</h1>

	<div class="prose">
		<p>Hi, I'm Pragathi.</p>
		<p>
			I have spent the past 10 years building software, intelligent systems and digital products,
			from embedded engineering and applied AI to mobile applications, backend systems and complete
			product releases.
		</p>
		<p>
			Before working independently, I held engineering roles at Bosch and Mercedes-Benz. My work
			covered computer vision, gaze and pose systems, multimodal AI, explainable AI, transformer and
			speech-based solutions, and the data and evaluation infrastructure underneath them. I studied
			Communication Engineering at TU Munich and completed my thesis on applying AI to radar.
		</p>
		<p>
			Today, I divide my time between building Anovi and taking on selected consulting and freelance
			projects across applied AI, software engineering and product development.
		</p>
		<p>
			I started Anovi because of a gap I kept running into: nutrition advice is often accurate and
			rarely usable. It does not account for what is already in your kitchen, what is expiring, what
			you have time to cook or what you actually enjoy eating. The interesting problem was never
			simply the model. It was translating evidence into a decision someone could make on a Tuesday
			evening.
		</p>
		<p>
			Building Anovi independently meant taking responsibility for the entire product: the
			architecture, database schema, recommendation logic, LLM pipeline, mobile experience,
			payments, localisation, privacy work and App Store release.
		</p>
		<p>
			That range is why this site exists. Building across disciplines taught me things worth
			documenting, and many of them are not the polished lessons that make it into conference talks.
		</p>
		<p>
			What I write here follows one rule: every claim has a receipt. When there is an upstream issue,
			I link to it. When there is not, I show the reproduction, measurement or control that supports
			the conclusion. That includes the approaches I abandoned, the systems that failed and the
			detectors that produced false positives.
		</p>
		<p>
			I write for people who care not only about whether technology works, but why it works, where
			it breaks and what it takes to make it dependable.
		</p>
	</div>

	<dl class="facts">
		{
			FACTS.map(([label, value]) => (
				<div>
					<dt>{label}</dt>
					<dd>{value}</dd>
				</div>
			))
		}
	</dl>

	<p class="links">
		<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>Email</a>
		<a href={SOCIAL.github} rel="me noopener">GitHub</a>
		<a href={SOCIAL.linkedin} rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>
	</p>
</Base>

<style>
	.facts {
		margin: 2.5rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
	}

	.facts div {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.25rem 1rem;
		padding-block: 0.6rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
	}

	dt {
		flex: 0 0 9rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}

	dd {
		margin: 0;
		flex: 1 1 16rem;
	}

	.links {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		font-size: 0.9375rem;
	}
</style>
